 ## Overview
-Style Loss is a regularization term used in differentiable volume rendering to improve color and style coherence between generated objects (or rendered scenes) and a given reference image [S1]. It operates by minimizing the distance between feature representations of the rendered output and the reference in a pre-trained VGG feature space [S1]. Unlike [Perceptual Loss](13426-perceptual-loss.md), which minimizes the distance to a fixed reference feature to preserve geometric and semantic integrity, Style Loss focuses on texture statistics and local contextual matching to enforce stylistic similarity [S1, 2].
